\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Archived single-chain $\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ m_\nu $ runs. Percentiles are empirical summaries of the stored samples after removing the first 20\% of rows. ``First half'' and ``second half'' are chronological halves of the retained chain. Split $\hat  R$ and the effective-sample-size proxy are classical scalar diagnostics. None of these runs meets the convergence criteria of \cref  {sec:mnu-inference}, so the percentiles are not posterior bounds.}}{12}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
